<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">09032026</say-as>.</s>
<s>The twentieth of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s>
<s>It is morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Israeli airstrikes set five oil facilities near Tehran ablaze on day thirteen of the Iran-Israel war, filling the capital with smoke so thick that residents were using headlights at noon — Iran's Red Crescent is warning of chemical burns and lung damage from the toxic air.</s>
<s>Brent crude has settled above one hundred and ten dollars a barrel as Iran's nine-day closure of the Strait of Hormuz continues to block a fifth of all seaborne oil.</s>
<s>Iran struck military bases across the Gulf overnight and named a new supreme leader under bombardment.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iranian drones struck the United States Fifth Fleet headquarters in Bahrain and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɑl uːˈdeɪd">Al Udeid</phoneme> Air Base in Qatar overnight, wounding thirty-two in Bahrain — four critically — while a separate strike on Riyadh killed two migrant workers.</s>
<s>Iran also struck a desalination plant in Bahrain; four hundred such plants along Gulf coasts supply forty percent of the world's desalinated water, and hundreds more across Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates remain within range.</s>
<s>None of the Gulf states has signaled willingness to expel American forces, despite being drawn into the fire.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Lebanon, Israeli forces landed by helicopter in the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="bɪˈkɑː">Bekaa</phoneme> Valley via Syrian territory, opening an eastern front as Lebanese authorities counted three hundred and ninety-four people killed since March second — eighty-three of them children.</s>
<s>Israeli tanks are advancing toward Christian villages in the south, and four hundred and fifty-four thousand people have been displaced in under two weeks.</s>
<s>The Lebanon front is expanding in near-silence while the world's attention stays on Tehran.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Armed Israeli settlers killed three Palestinians at <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɪrˈbɛt ɑˈbuː fɑˈlɑ">Khirbet Abu Falah</phoneme> under the protection of Israeli army forces, as settler violence has surged twenty-five percent since the Iran war began.</s>
<s>Israeli military units have been redeployed from the occupied West Bank to other fronts, leaving settlers effectively unsupervised.</s>
<s>Eight Palestinians have been killed by settlers in twelve days.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Sudan expelled every United Nations agency from the town of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɑˈkoʊ.boʊ">Akobo</phoneme> before advancing army troops into the area — a pattern of clearing international witnesses ahead of military operations documented in Sudan, Myanmar, and Ethiopia.</s>
<s>Thousands are now fleeing toward the Ethiopian border.</s>
<s>No humanitarian organization remains to record what follows.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Under Israeli bombardment, Iran's Assembly of Experts named <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="modʒˈtɑː.bɑ kɑˈmeɪ.niː">Mojtaba Khamenei</phoneme> supreme leader — a hereditary appointment that breaks forty-seven years of precedent, made in defiance of a public death threat from United States President Donald Trump.</s>
<s>Iran's Health Ministry reports twelve hundred dead in the war so far, among them two hundred women and children.</s>
<s>The choice of who leads Iran now will shape whether this conflict is negotiated, escalated, or simply endured.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistani police arrested fourteen <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈɔː.rɑt">Aurat</phoneme> March activists in Islamabad on International Women's Day, invoking a ban on public gatherings after a prominent mosque threatened to block the procession.</s>
<s>Among those detained was rights activist Dr <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fɑrˈzɑː.nɑ bɑˈriː">Farzana Bari</phoneme>; lawyers who arrived to represent the detainees were also taken into custody.</s>
<s>The crackdown shows how religious pressure and state authority in Pakistan increasingly move as one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Colombia's centrist parties collapsed in Sunday's congressional vote, with President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɡuˈstɑː.voʊ ˈpɛ.troʊ">Gustavo Petro</phoneme>'s left-wing coalition taking the most seats at twenty-two percent, closely followed by former president <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈɑl.vɑ.roʊ uˈriː.beɪ">Álvaro Uribe</phoneme>'s right-wing party at fifteen.</s>
<s>Congress is now split twenty-four ways, leaving Petro — who cannot seek re-election in May — unable to advance land reform or peace negotiations without building an unlikely coalition.</s>
<s>Latin America's political center is hollowing out.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Bangladesh closed every university in the country after the Hormuz blockade doubled the cost of liquefied natural gas, leaving a hundred and seventy million people without power in a nation that imports ninety-five percent of its energy.</s>
<s>Fuel rationing is in force, with no restart date set beyond <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːd ɑl ˈfɪ.tɚ">Eid al-Fitr</phoneme>.</s>
<s>Bangladesh did not choose this war; it is paying for it regardless.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iraq's oil output has fallen seventy percent since the conflict began — from four million barrels a day to one-point-three million — as the Hormuz closure blocks all Gulf export terminals.</s>
<s>The Iraqi government has no alternative export route and no timeline for restoring hospital budgets or civil service salaries for forty-three million people.</s>
<s>A country that played no part in starting this war is among its most economically devastated.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Flooding killed twenty-three people in Nairobi and forced the closure of the city's international airport, the latest consequence of intensifying rainfall across East Africa driven by warming in the Indian Ocean.</s>
<s>Nairobi's drainage has not kept pace with decades of rapid population growth, leaving informal settlements built on floodplains with no protection.</s>
<s>Kenya has announced no plan to relocate those communities.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Scientists have grown millimeter-scale crystals of hexagonal diamond — a form of carbon theoretically fifty-eight percent harder than ordinary diamond — marking the first time this material has been produced at usable scale.</s>
<s>Previous attempts yielded only atom-thin traces; the team says bulk <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈlɒnz.dəl.aɪt">lonsdaleite</phoneme> could enable harder cutting tools and high-pressure scientific applications.</s>
<s>A material theorized for decades has finally been made real at a size you can hold.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Social media platform X was paying creators through its ad-revenue program to post artificial-intelligence-generated war footage without labeling it as synthetic — content that earned engagement precisely because audiences believed it was real.</s>
<s>One fabricated clip of missiles striking Jerusalem's Dome of the Rock was shared thousands of times from a verified account.</s>
<s>X now says accounts that post unlabeled synthetic content will lose creator payouts for ninety days, with enforcement relying on user reports.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Vietnam passed the first binding artificial intelligence law in Southeast Asia, choosing enforceable regulation while neighboring Indonesia, Thailand, and the Philippines rely only on voluntary guidelines.</s>
<s>No Association of Southeast Asian Nations-wide framework exists, and Vietnam's law sets a precedent that the region's other governments will now face pressure to match or explain.</s>
<s>The move marks a split between countries that regulate before harm occurs and those that wait.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We return this evening, as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme> reaches <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑːɡɹɪb">Maghrib</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>